## Recovery Contract

- Missing or duplicated registration assignment fails report construction and blocks release.
- Unknown origins remain cohort errors; valid direct origins remain controlled Direct Work2 work.
- Legacy reports show unavailable or unverified grouping rather than a false empty backlog.
- Normalized-equivalent release tags fail for explicit resolution.
- Base correction is preview-only until an exact working-cohort manifest is applied; frozen and
  later cohorts refuse correction.
- Any failed local, CI, platform, publication, production, dashboard, or client-sync check leaves
  the governing outcome and cohort open.

## Verification Strategy

- Unit and property-style tests for partition completeness, overlapping commits, direct/document
  mixtures, overflow aggregation, schema compatibility, privacy allowlists, and state separation.
- Focused reporter, hosted contract/view, local status, release-cohort, tag, repair, and Work5
  selection tests.
- Strict Doctor and full release-profile validation.
- Configured development and production web, Windows, and Linux lane evidence.
- Exact content-SHA GitHub CI, provenance/tag/Release verification, hosted convergence, and exact
  installed-client source parity.
